      "value": "@{5de9405aea7cc52772fcc359|full_name}: Sure! I mulled over a few terms that might be more easily understand by your average user. \nBoolean: Probably better visualized as Switch given it's on/off; yes/no behavior. I don't think I ever heard this term before learning some basic C#. \nFloat: Another term I never heard until learning some programming. Might be better understood as a Decimal Number or a Number Fraction. \nInt/Integer: People might understand that this refers to a number, but it might be clearer if stated as a Whole Number. \nBlock: I would have never guessed that a Block is what would let me distribute the same command to other nodes. To me a block is a thing that halts or stops something. I think Redirect or Distribute would illustrate that better.\nI haven't constructed something in Udon needing For or While loops yet, but here's some possible alternatives that's clearer from the start.\nFor: Though okay, I think Duration or For Duration would get the point across quicker. \nWhile: I'm not sure what could replace this at the moment as it's okay as a term, but still not totally clear from the first look what it's for. In addition, I got a glimpse of this node and don't think any average person will understand what \"Body\" is supposed to denote as one of the branches out. \nThis all of course could use a ton of workshopping and there is likely a ton of other properties that could stand further clarification, but it's what I've mused over at the moment.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
