      "value": "@{5ca510162225c760a69dd9a3|full_name}: \nNothing in a programming environment is going to be easy for people who don't know anything about it.\nBut most of these renames will, as I see it, just cause more confusion as they collide with other names or make it sound like it means something else.\nI can see why Block can probably be confusing, but the other renames will cause even more confusion as they collide with other names that already exists in C#.\nThe best bet is to just get a really basic understanding of what these things mean.\nI.e For loops, if that is renamed to Duration (which makes it sound like it's based on time/clock) will just make it even more difficult to read up on and understand. Since it doesn't match up with anything and would show you a result that doesn't have anything to do with it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
