      "value": "@{5ca510162225c760a69dd9a3|full_name} - thanks for listing out your ideas - as a programmer, it's helpful to understand what terms might trip up those with less programming experience.\nI think it's important to learn some basic programming terms if you want to write programs - I think a lot of programming is just figuring out how to break problems down into smaller parts until you can solve each of those parts. Learning how loops work is fundamental to solving many problems - if you can describe your problem as a set of items that need to be processed, then you know you can use one of these tools to solve it!\nIt sounds like it would be helpful to have documentation (video,article,etc) describing the building blocks and what some of these terms mean. A big advantage in learning these terms is that they're pretty universal in programming - booleans, floats, ints, loops - these are found everywhere and will help you understand all sorts of code.\nI agree with you about the Block node - it's specific to node-based programming and to Udon in particular, and there may be a better name for it, or at least some solid examples showing how it works.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
